    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1986-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The second factor \\(40.3 + 0.07 = 40.37\\) is about \\(40,\\) and \\(1.8\\) is about \\(2.\\) A quick estimate is \\(2(40) - 0.2(40) = 80 - 8 = 72,\\) so the product is closest to \\(74.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "Round each factor: \\(1.8\\) is near \\(2\\) and \\(40.3 + 0.07\\) is near \\(40\\)",
        "Estimate \\(2 \\times 40\\) and adjust slightly downward since \\(1.8 \\lt 2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
